.TH WREX-ARP 7 "2026-10-18" "wrex 0.1.0" "wrex Manual"
.SH NAME
wrex-arp \- arp layer for \fBwrex\fR(1)

.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBwrex\fR \fIcraft\fR|\fIsend\fR [options] \fB--layer\fR \fIarp\fR \fB--arp\-<field>\fR=\fIVALUE\fR ...
\fBwrex\fR \fIfields\fR \fIarp\fR

.SH DESCRIPTION
Address Resolution Protocol (RFC 826) for Ethernet: fixed 28\-byte request/reply header (htype=1 Ethernet, ptype=0x0800 IPv4, hlen=6, plen=4). oper: 1=request, 2=reply. Terminal layer; carries no next\-header chain. Stacks on eth or vlan (802.1Q tag). tpa is required: crafting without it is an Unfillable error.
.

.SH ENCAPSULATION
Rank 20; stacks on eth, vlan (parents).

.SH "FIELD FLAGS"
Dots in field paths become dashes in flags (ipv4.ttl -> --ipv4-ttl, --arp-htype).
Explicit values always win over autofill and are kept
unvalidated; \fB\-\-strict\fR re-validates (violations exit 2).
.TP
\fB\-\-arp\-htype=\fIINT\fR\fR
hardware type (autofill: 1 ethernet) Type u16. Default: 1.
.TP
\fB\-\-arp\-ptype=\fIINT\fR\fR
protocol type (autofill: 0x0800 ipv4) Type u16. Default: 2048.
.TP
\fB\-\-arp\-hlen=\fIINT\fR\fR
hardware address length (autofill: 6) Type u8. Default: 6.
.TP
\fB\-\-arp\-plen=\fIINT\fR\fR
protocol address length (autofill: 4) Type u8. Default: 4.
.TP
\fB\-\-arp\-oper=\fIINT\fR\fR
operation (autofill: 1 request) Type u16. Default: 1.
.TP
\fB\-\-arp\-sha=\fIMAC\fR\fR
sender hardware address (autofill: 00:00:00:00:00:00) Type mac. Default: 00:00:00:00:00:00.
.TP
\fB\-\-arp\-spa=\fIIP\fR\fR
sender protocol address Type ipv4. Default: 0.0.0.0.
.TP
\fB\-\-arp\-tha=\fIMAC\fR\fR
target hardware address (autofill: 00:00:00:00:00:00) Type mac. Default: 00:00:00:00:00:00.
.TP
\fB\-\-arp\-tpa=\fIIP\fR\fR
target protocol address (required) Type ipv4. Default: 0.0.0.0. Required.

.SH EXAMPLES
wrex craft \-\-format hex \-\-layer eth \-\-layer arp \\\\
  \-\-arp\-oper=1 \-\-arp\-tpa=10.0.0.1
# arp.tpa is required: omitting it is an Unfillable error

.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBwrex\fR(1), \fBwrex\-eth\fR(7), \fBwrex\-vlan\fR(7), \fBwrex\-ipv4\fR(7), \fBwrex\-icmp\fR(7), \fBwrex\-udp\fR(7), \fBwrex\-tcp\fR(7), \fBwrex\-dns\fR(7)
